{"title":"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Solution_1_but_simpler)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Solution 1 but simpler)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Efficient_[4],_Not_as_good_as_[1])\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Efficient [4], Not as good as [1])</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Education,_the_Study_of_Everything\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Education, the Study of Everything</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the hundreds digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23bf9752a006bdb45586e6d015876dd7681db7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20!-15!)?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d76eff7a656b21dd2cb3d3ab1ca32124c70e8c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }0\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }1\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }4\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec0dcde3e88efde55a8c8df29fc970f9e6c6da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/4821bef1583b2c97354f97e80940f15c079a0fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe8ffbaf55875f55dd581143da6b8bb90c376b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, the last three digits of both numbers is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this means that the difference of the hundreds digits is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ea1f26eedb2d601fdd27e52e6dc0e5f4b4be7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can clearly see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58b9df707d7991a4231f112b55c1295380b6e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20! \\equiv 15! \\equiv 0 \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa2dbd615214fcf2e542f45680caf96b6f44495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20! - 15! \\equiv 0 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"20\" /> meaning that the last two digits are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f2c746327924273ba209f0879ea846a0b8dd6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$00$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and the hundreds digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3da52b01338a780e88792a26c3f95dc74f44f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>--abhinavg0627\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 3 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebb3ad20c08f2f4313b00ea2b5a52a05c3ea05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20!= 2432902008176640000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"222\" height=\"14\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd023dda71bbeb02896b95e31f037dc9e2684da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15!= 1307674368000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Then, we see that the hundreds digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c4931f24581a632fb3a3e6ffae6d5c4e7b7ac17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0-0=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~dragoon\n</p><p>Please do not do this and only use this solution as a last resort.\n</p><p>Note for people not used to comp. math: This is a completely reasonable way to solve this problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Solution_1_but_simpler.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Solution_1_but_simpler)\">Solution 4 (Solution 1 but simpler)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Solution 1 but simpler)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/4821bef1583b2c97354f97e80940f15c079a0fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> (it is easier than it seems) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/69194c2455b7d07137310cb922981da331e02d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{11} * 3^6 * 5^3 * 7^2 * 11 * 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"197\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Notice that it includes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a742dd93a866a82d70b6264de594cb0deb28751d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 * 5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> which is 1000\n</p><p>Therefore 15! and 20! are both multiples of 1000, the hundreds place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3da52b01338a780e88792a26c3f95dc74f44f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ Someone\n</p><p><b>Remark:</b>\n</p><p>Although you state this as simpler (which maybe for those not fluent in number theory for amc, it is), this is not the best solution. That title is still awarded to solution 1. I place a variation of your solution below which is more efficient than this, but definitely nowhere near Solution 1.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Efficient_.5B4.5D.2C_Not_as_good_as_.5B1.5D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Efficient_[4],_Not_as_good_as_[1])\">Solution 5 (Efficient [4], Not as good as [1])</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Efficient [4], Not as good as [1])\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of 1000 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df24896effb4c9f0869b965bc4c1cdd0dec695ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 \\cdot 5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a8161760db62f0f07e4792d70ebc390aaec54850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a26e991024c3c02bd15af389ff2f8a107fb31ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec0dcde3e88efde55a8c8df29fc970f9e6c6da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe8ffbaf55875f55dd581143da6b8bb90c376b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by 1000. Similarly, in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/4821bef1583b2c97354f97e80940f15c079a0fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, we already have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec0dcde3e88efde55a8c8df29fc970f9e6c6da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a26e991024c3c02bd15af389ff2f8a107fb31ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41754b5ef316bef640df43e9d3d853d52660b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 4 = 2^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/4821bef1583b2c97354f97e80940f15c079a0fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is also divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, both are divisible by 1000, and thus end in 000, and when you subtract these, you obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d91c030ce48013e9bda991a5838fda903041f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{0}00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Education.2C_the_Study_of_Everything\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Education,_the_Study_of_Everything\">Video Solution by Education, the Study of Everything</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Education, the Study of Everything\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/J4Bqztwjyxw\">https://youtu.be/J4Bqztwjyxw</a>\n</p><p>~Education, The Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/V1fY0oLSHvo\">https://youtu.be/V1fY0oLSHvo</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=3899\">https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=3899</a>\n</p><p>~pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A\">2019 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017142223\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 271/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5525/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.081      1 -total\n 60.13%    7.865      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.95%    5.095      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17208:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017142223 and revision id 293793. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}